Yet Another Silly YANI:

A box of sidewalk chalk. Provides a fast, one-use, semi-permanent
means of writing Elbereth. A box will contain up to 10 sticks of
chalk. Each piece of chalk can (E)ngrave up to 8 letters in a single
turn. Once a stick of chalk is used to engrave a message of any
length, the extra is discarded (i.e. no saving half-used chalk bits.)
The message will be written in a random color (no significance, just
adds to the silliness.) It will remain until erased, either
deliberately, or by water. Any contact with water on the square will
erase the message: this includes potions that smash on the floor
beside you, pools created on the square, a water elemental, steam
vortex, fog cloud, or other water-based creature passing over the
square, etc.

